  "interpretation": [
    "Fixed worker full matrix retains slab4 regression (~7.6%) and buddy2 median variation; do not report universal improvement.",
    "Identical first-pool slab4 diagnostic yields median153.3ns in both versions over9 pairs with matching size and address phases. Sequential143vs153ns is not reproduced when allocation history is controlled.",
    "First-pool buddy2 diagnostic reverses direction (330.3ns original vs273.5ns TLS), with different page offsets. This demonstrates sensitivity to process allocation history/address placement; does not prove a universal speedup.",
    "TLS optimization removes4 transient CacheShard Arc counter operations per allocate/free pair, adds no locks/heap allocations on hits, and materially improves uncontended and2-thread slab latency.",
    "Production benchmark now supports RUAPC_BENCH_CPU_BASE, RUAPC_BENCH_SIZE and RUAPC_BENCH_THREADS for per-case reproduction. Diagnostic address logging exists only in /tmp harnesses."
  ],
  "excluded_datasets": [
    "ruapc-bufpool-final-contention-*.log and ruapc-bufpool-final-lazy_merge-*.log are rejected parking_lot experiment comparisons, not final production data",
    "ruapc-probe-current and its current column were stale diagnostic builds",
    "Earlier standard/state matrices predate latest TLS and have different process placement; retain as history, not headline evidence"
  ]
